<title>MEXICO: BANCO DE MEXICO COMPLETES SECONDARY OPERATIONS.</title>
<headline>BANCO DE MEXICO COMPLETES SECONDARY OPERATIONS.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico placed all three direct sales of paper and five repurchase agreements through wich it had sought to drain 2.449 billion pesos from the secondary market on Friday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    359 days   20.91 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    180 days   20.85 pct</p>
<p>    150 million     90 days   19.81 pct</p>
<p>The terms and amounts of the repurchase agreements were placed as follows:</p>
<p>    590 million     45 days   20.49 pct</p>
<p>    400 million     38 days   20.30 pct</p>
<p>    400 million     21 days   20.19 pct</p>
<p>    500 million     13 days   20.17 pct</p>
<p>    109 million	3 days   20.00 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
